WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:02.880
The whole world is watching the&nbsp;
Falcon and the Winter Soldier&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:04.800
continue their fight against the Flag-Smashers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:09.120
as the increasingly-unhinged John Walker&nbsp;
continues to tarnish Captain America's shield.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:13.200
Here's some of the easter eggs you may have missed&nbsp;
in The Falcon and the Winter Soldier episode four.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:17.920
In the first act of "The Whole World is Watching,"&nbsp;
Sam, Bucky, and Zemo try to get information&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:22.480
on Donya Madani, Karli's deceased adoptive&nbsp;
mother. It's a dead-end for Sam and Bucky,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:26.560
as the duo seem to scare off everyone they&nbsp;
come in contact with. Sam does manage to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:31.200
have one brief conversation with a refugee, but&nbsp;
he refuses to give up any information on Donya.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:35.920
Then we see Zemo outside, approaching a group&nbsp;
of children while singing "Baa Baa Black Sheep."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:39.840
He dumps a pile of candy in front of them —&nbsp;
the same Turkish delight he mentioned to Bucky&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:44.240
and Sam, inside the Latvian apartment. He tells&nbsp;
the group of kids that the candy was his son's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:48.880
favorite. Zemo uses the sweets as a way to dazzle&nbsp;
the youngsters and get information out of them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:53.360
It works like a charm: The little girl reveals&nbsp;
when and where Donya's funeral will be.

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:57.760
While this seems like the sort of simple, clever&nbsp;
tactic you might see on an episode of Law &amp; Order,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:01.280
Zemo's use of the candy actually has a&nbsp;
connection to another fictional universe.

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:03.840
"Turkish delight."

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.080
Turkish delight is the candy the&nbsp;
White Witch uses in The Chronicles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:12.000
of Narnia to get information out of Edmund&nbsp;
Pevensie. It's Edmund's favorite candy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:15.760
but the White Witch's sweets are also&nbsp;
enchanted, making them impossible to resist.

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:19.600
In "The Whole World is Watching," we&nbsp;
finally get to see the Winter Soldier&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:22.800
in all his blade-wielding glory.&nbsp;
During the high-octane fight with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:25.840
the Flag Smashers at their home&nbsp;
base, Bucky shows off his skills,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:29.840
notably his ability to throw and catch a&nbsp;
knife by its handle like it's no big deal.

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:33.360
The move is a nod to Captain America: The&nbsp;
Winter Soldier, with Bucky replicating a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:37.760
move he used on Steve Rogers during the&nbsp;
street fight scene in the 2014 movie.

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:41.200
In "The Whole World is Watching," Bucky's&nbsp;
knife does a couple more spins than it does&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:44.880
in the film. Both scenes, however, show&nbsp;
off just how slick Bucky's skills are.

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:48.240
"What's with all the knives?"

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:52.880
This display of skill is yet another instance of&nbsp;
the series referencing the MCU's most memorable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:57.360
moments. It should also be noted that this moment&nbsp;
shows Bucky's growth as a character, as he is not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:01.760
willing to kill, which is why he throws the knife&nbsp;
next to his opponent's head, and not through it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:06.080
Back when we first met him in The Winter Soldier,&nbsp;
in contrast, he had no problem with ending a life.

00:02:07.037 --> 00:02:11.600
In "The Whole World is Watching," Walker kills a&nbsp;
Flag Smasher by driving his shield into his chest.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:15.360
This gives us one of the series' most&nbsp;
eerie shots: John Walker seen from below,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:20.240
as he holds a bloody shield. This specifically&nbsp;
invokes a prior moment in Steve Rogers' history,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:24.160
making it all the more clear how dramatically&nbsp;
the old Cap differs from the new Cap.

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:28.000
In Captain America: Civil War's final&nbsp;
battle, Steve uses his shield to smash&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:32.160
Iron Man's helmet. Instead of landing a&nbsp;
blow to the head, as the audience expects,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:36.320
Cap digs his shield into Tony's arc reactor,&nbsp;
which puts his suit out of commission. Steve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:40.640
easily could have killed or seriously injured&nbsp;
Tony in that moment, but that's not who he is.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:44.240
He uses his shield as a way to subdue&nbsp;
his opponent, instead of killing him.

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:47.360
The Falcon and the Winter Soldier&nbsp;
employs cinematography reminiscent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:51.120
of what's used in that Civil War scene,&nbsp;
making for a unique and potent callback.

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:55.360
Walker doesn't have a personal history with&nbsp;
this Flag Smasher, as Steve does with Tony,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:58.640
but he also doesn't have the ability to&nbsp;
stop himself and assess the situation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:00.320
which makes him highly dangerous.

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:04.000
There's a darkness inside of Walker, which&nbsp;
has been emphasized by the Super-Soldier&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:07.360
serum running through his veins. Steve&nbsp;
doesn't have that darkness in him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:10.480
making him a much better&nbsp;
Captain America on all fronts.

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:11.680
"That shield doesn't belong to you."

00:03:12.911 --> 00:03:15.711
"You don't deserve it!"

